# ── PARAMETER WORDLIST FUZZING (v10.14 — hidden GET param discovery)
# The crawler only finds parameters that appear in HTML (<a href="?x=1">,
# <form>, src=). PHP apps reading $_GET['attachment'] directly are
# structurally invisible to a crawl-based scanner — the param works even
# though nothing links to it. This is the #1 source of false negatives vs
# nuclei's top-xss-params template (estrava case: /estrava/stara/?attachment=
# is vulnerable on a never-linked param). This module batch-probes a curated
# wordlist of ~350 common param names against param-less endpoints, detects
# which canaries reflect, and feeds the live params back into the normal
# scan pipeline as if the crawler had found them. Detection-only — the
# existing context-aware / fuzzer phases do the actual XSS testing.
